The Cheney family are as fiercely private about the case today as they were in 1994. Despite the flawed forensics, they still believe there is enough circumstantial evidence against Henry Keough to warrant a retrial. The Cheneys were never consulted about the nolly prosecwee. A statement released by their lawyer in 2018 said a retrial was their only hope for closure. It's a case that continues to divide the public. Some call it one of the biggest miscarriages of justice Australia has ever seen, while others think a guilty man walks free.
